From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Buldygin <froooks@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hal/h264e/vepu540c: read back int_sta hw status register

The H.264 VEPU 540C HAL only registered a read-back request for the
status class (reg_st at VEPU540C_STATUS_OFFSET) before submitting the
task, but hal_h264e_vepu540c_status_check() inspects
reg_ctl.common.int_sta.enc_done_sta, which lives in the control class at
offset VEPU540C_REG_BASE_HW_STATUS (0x2c) and was therefore never fetched
from the kernel.

The rkvenc2 kernel driver deliberately injects the saved hardware
interrupt status into that register on task completion ("revert hack for
irq status" in rkvenc_finish()), but that value is only copied back to
user space for register ranges that user space asked to read. Because the
control class was written but never read, status_check() always saw
int_sta == 0 and reported:

  hal_h264e_vepu540c: hal_h264e_vepu540c_status_check enc not done \
      hw_status: 0x00000000

even though the encoder completed every frame normally (kernel logs
"irq_status: 00000001" = enc_done, no timeout, no error). Each frame was
then discarded with size 0.

The H.265 (H265eV540cStatusElem) and VEPU 580 H.264 HALs already read the
int_sta register back explicitly; mirror the VEPU 580 sequence here by
adding the missing MPP_DEV_REG_RD for reg_ctl.common.int_sta at
VEPU540C_REG_BASE_HW_STATUS before the status-class read-back.

This is most visible on encoder-only SoCs such as RV1106/RV1103, where
mpi_enc_test is the primary bring-up test.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 mpp/hal/rkenc/h264e/hal_h264e_vepu540c.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mpp/hal/rkenc/h264e/hal_h264e_vepu540c.c b/mpp/hal/rkenc/h264e/hal_h264e_vepu540c.c
index ab0fac447..d5e339c4c 100644
--- a/mpp/hal/rkenc/h264e/hal_h264e_vepu540c.c
+++ b/mpp/hal/rkenc/h264e/hal_h264e_vepu540c.c
@@ -1590,6 +1590,16 @@ static MPP_RET hal_h264e_vepu540c_gen_regs(void *hal, HalEncTask *task)
             break;
         }
 
+        rd_cfg.reg = &ctx->regs_set->reg_ctl.common.int_sta;
+        rd_cfg.size = sizeof(RK_U32);
+        rd_cfg.offset = VEPU540C_REG_BASE_HW_STATUS;
+
+        ret = mpp_dev_ioctl(ctx->dev, MPP_DEV_REG_RD, &rd_cfg);
+        if (ret) {
+            mpp_err_f("set register read failed %d\n", ret);
+            break;
+        }
+
         rd_cfg.reg = &ctx->regs_set->reg_st;
         rd_cfg.size = sizeof(ctx->regs_set->reg_st);
         rd_cfg.offset = VEPU540C_STATUS_OFFSET;
-- 
